{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015cHx3kfCHvvqcpmMvWdzCr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Phase 2 â€” Execution Log\n2\t\n3\tForeman records per-wave build outcomes below. 8 wave(s) planned\n4\t(Wave 1-2 = security hardening H1-H2; Wave 3-8 = llm.py upgrades L1-L6).\n5\t\n6\t## Waves\n7\t\n8\t### Wave 1 â€” H1: Payload-depth security scan â€” GREEN (2026-06-06)\n9\t\n10\t- **Deliverable:** `bin/scan_payload_depth.py` â€” re-fetches each scannable artifact's\n11\t  payload (payloads not retained on disk; reuses `fetcher` 7-day cache) and runs the real\n12\t  `payload_extractor.extract â†’ detectors â†’ scorer.score` path, persisting via\n13\t  `gate.write_verdict` in enforce mode. Monotonic re-stamp guard delegates to\n14\t  `gate._worst_status` (worst-wins; never raises servability). `--limit/--dry-run/--audit-out`.\n15\t- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 799 passed (793 after EXECUTE, +6 after FIX; baseline 752).\n16\t  No test weakening. No new `security_status IN (...)` literal (single-owner test green).\n17\t- **Review:** 2 independent reviewers. R1 GO (no blocker). R2 GO with 2 MAJORs:\n18\t  F1 (non-GitHub zero-byte fetch falsely labeled `payload-depth`), F2 (errors didn't gate\n19\t  exit/coverage). FIX iter 1 closed both + 2 MINORs; closure VERIFIER mutation-tested each\n20\t  fix â†’ all CLOSED, invariants intact â†’ GO.\n21\t- **Honesty fix (F1):** only genuinely fetched-and-scanned artifacts get `scan_depth:\n22\t  payload-depth`; no-payload artifacts (â‰ˆ506/775, mostly arxiv) get `served-text-fallback`\n23\t  and keep their monotonic value (not newly quarantined). Coverage breakdown in the audit.\n24\t- **SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED (not run):** the live re-stamp against kb/aurora.db. Build delivers\n25\t  the CLI + tests only.\n26\t\n27\t### Wave 2 â€” H2: Evidence-loop promotion machinery â€” GREEN (2026-06-06)\n28\t\n29\t- **Deliverables:** real per-iteration LLM `make_live_score_fn` in `roles/evidence.py`\n30\t  (re-runs critic_a/b/c+reconciler over the deepened corpus, metered, never writes the\n31\t  verdict, guards verbatim); `bin/engine-diff.py` (GO/NO-GO enforcing agreementâ‰¥0.95,\n32\t  samplesâ‰¥200, unearned==0, costâ‰¤1.5Ã—, strict profile additive); `bin/run_evidence_shadow.py`\n33\t  (budget-capped metered batch â€” SA-1 machinery, not run live); default-off live engine switch\n34\t  `AURORA_EVIDENCE_ENGINE=legacy|loop`.\n35\t- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 832 passed, 1 pre-existing skip (824 after EXECUTE, +8 after\n36\t  FIX). No test weakening.\n37\t- **Review:** 2 reviewers. Both agreed (â‰¥2 â†’ BLOCKER-class) the nightly shadow path had been\n38\t  swapped to the real score_fn, silently adding per-candidate LLM cost; R2 also reproduced a\n39\t  $0-shadow cost-gate GO. NO-GO â†’ FIX iter 1 closed: nightly defaults to ZERO-cost\n40\t  precomputed score_fn (real re-score behind default-off `AURORA_EVIDENCE_LIVE_RESCORE`);\n41\t  $0-shadow â†’ NO-GO; `evidence_shadow` budget cell; live-switch adoption now monotonic-toward-\n42\t  stricter vs legacy (fail-safe). Closure VERIFIER mutation-tested all â†’ GO.\n43\t- **TRIPWIRE / follow-up:** R2-4 candidate-filter (non-empty bundle) works but lacks a dedicated\n44\t  regression test (LOW). \n45\t- **SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED (not run):** SA-1 (metered shadow batch to populate validations_shadow\n46\t  â‰¥200) and SA-2 (live `AURORA_EVIDENCE_ENGINE=loop` flip). Default stays legacy; nightly stays\n47\t  zero added cost.\n48\t\n49\t### Wave 3 â€” L1: Cost-telemetry substrate â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n50\t\n51\t- **Deliverables:** migration `0024_costs_cache_batch.sql` (+ schema.sql mirror) adding nullable\n52\t  `cache_read_tokens`/`cache_write_tokens`/`batch_mode` to `costs`; `kb/pricing.yaml` cache\n53\t  sub-rates (cache_read â‰ˆ0.1Ã—, cache_write â‰ˆ1.25Ã—) for sonnet-4-6 + haiku-4-5 + `batch_discount:\n54\t  0.5`, all provenance-flagged `verified:false`; `llm.py` `lookup_cache_rates`/`batch_discount` +\n55\t  `CostRecorder.record(... cache_read_tokens=0, cache_write_tokens=0, batch_mode=False)` â€” legacy\n56\t  4-arg path byte-for-byte unchanged.\n57\t- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 845 passed (+13). No test weakening.\n58\t- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. R1 nothing found (legacy unchanged to the cent verified;\n59\t  migration idempotent + applies clean to a live-DB copy preserving 22,013 rows). R2 GO + 5/5\n60\t  mutation-caught tests; one LOW (F2: structural non-slash skip in the verification test) â€”\n61\t  orchestrator-applied an explicit `_NON_RATE_VERIFICATION_KEYS` allowlist so a slash-dropping\n62\t  typo fails loudly; re-gated green.\n63\t- **Note:** migration authored + tested; applied to the live DB by the normal migrate runner (not\n64\t  hand-mutated in the build).\n65\t\n66\t### Wave 4 â€” L2: Prompt caching â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n67\t\n68\t- **Deliverables:** `llm.py` `call_anthropic`/`call_model` gain `cache_system` (structured\n69\t  ephemeral system block, cache-read/write metered via L1); invariant rubric/schema moved into the\n70\t  cached system block for critic_a, reconciler, security judge; Sonnetâ†’Haiku fallback carries the\n71\t  marker; default (cache-off) path byte-for-byte unchanged.\n72\t- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 858 passed (854 after EXECUTE, +4 after FIX). No test weakening.\n73\t- **Review:** 2 reviewers. R1 GO (default unchanged, fallback caches, the 3 modified test mocks are\n74\t  faithful signature propagation not weakening). R2 GO with a HIGH efficacy finding (W4-R2-1):\n75\t  cached prefixes (65â€“317 tok) are far below Anthropic's per-model minimums (Sonnet 2048 / Haiku\n76\t  4096), so caching silently never fires. FIX iter 1: maximized the stable prefix (moved invariant\n77\t  rubric/schema into system â€” token-multiset identical, F6 fences intact), then GATED the marker\n78\t  behind `cache_prefix_clears_minimum` (no dead marker sent) and added honesty-pinning tests.\n79\t  Closure VERIFIER: judge content semantically identical (16/16), gating correct, no-op pin\n80\t  non-vacuous â†’ GO.\n81\t- **HONEST OUTCOME / TRIPWIRE:** prompt caching is a **no-op for Aurora's current prompt sizes** â€”\n82\t  all roles' stable prefixes are 15â€“60Ã— below the model minimum. The plumbing is correct and\n83\t  gated; it activates automatically only if a role's stable prefix ever exceeds the minimum. This\n84\t  refines the AuroraTwo research's #1 \"cheap win\" (it was corroboration-only; measured as\n85\t  inapplicable at current sizes). No cost savings banked.\n86\t\n87\t### Wave 5 â€” L3: Structured outputs â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n88\t\n89\t- **Deliverables:** `llm.py` `call_anthropic`/`call_model` gain `output_schema` via strict forced\n90\t  tool-use (`emit_result` tool whose input_schema IS the caller schema; SDK has no metering-safe\n91\t  native parse path); shared `CRITIC_VERDICT_SCHEMA`/`RECONCILED_VERDICT_SCHEMA` in contracts.py +\n92\t  `JUDGE_DECISION_SCHEMA`; critic_a/critic_b(Anthropic-fallback)/reconciler/judge pass schemas;\n93\t  Gemini path + langextract untouched. Off-schema judge â†’ abstain (fail-closed, enforced by\n94\t  `_parse_response`, not by `strict`).\n95\t- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 874 passed (869 after EXECUTE, +5 after FIX). No test weakening.\n96\t- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. R1 nothing found (fail-closed independently re-verified by the\n97\t  parser). R2 GO-conditional with W5-F1 (MEDIUM): no-`required` strict schema acceptance is\n98\t  unverified against the live API; a rejection would 400 on both Sonnet+Haiku and (since\n99\t  critic/reconciler weren't exception-wrapped) abort the nightly sweep. FIX iter 1: structured call\n100\t  now DEGRADES to a plain text call on any structured-call failure (metered once off the successful\n101\t  call, degrade logged) + defense-in-depth (critic_a/b/reconciler treat a hard call error as\n102\t  degrade-to-None). Closure VERIFIER mutation-tested all â†’ GO.\n103\t- **TRIPWIRE:** if the live API rejects the no-`required` strict schema, structured outputs silently\n104\t  degrade to the legacy plain-text parse (no benefit, no harm). A one-call live smoke against\n105\t  Sonnet/Haiku would confirm whether the schema activates; until then, treat L3 as best-effort.\n106\t\n107\t### Wave 6 â€” L4: Adaptive thinking via `effort` â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n108\t\n109\t- **Deliverables:** `call_anthropic`/`call_model` gain `effort` (maps to `thinking={\"type\":\"adaptive\"}`\n110\t  + `output_config={\"effort\": low|medium|high|xhigh|max}` per the claude-api skill); a recursive\n111\t  `_assert_no_budget_tokens` guard runs before EVERY Anthropic dispatch (initial + Haiku fallback +\n112\t  structuredâ†’plain degrade) â€” Opus 4.8 400s on budget_tokens; `_fold_thinking_into_output` folds any\n113\t  separately-reported thinking tokens into metered output (the $118 lesson). Default (effort unset) =\n114\t  cost-neutral, byte-for-byte unchanged. Gemini `thinking_budget=0` guard + `thoughts_token_count`\n115\t  fold untouched.\n116\t- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 891 passed (+17). No test weakening.\n117\t- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. Guard verified comprehensive + recursive (catches nested\n118\t  budget_tokens); fold matches Anthropic's real usage semantics (thinking already in output_tokens â†’\n119\t  fold is a correct no-op today, no double-count); mutation-resistant tests (fold-removal under-meter\n120\t  AND double-count over-meter both caught).\n121\t- **TRIPWIRES (LOW, latent, opt-in path only):** (1) the additive thinking-fold could *over*-meter if\n122\t  a future Anthropic usage field duplicates already-counted thinking tokens â€” no current field exists,\n123\t  forward-compat bet; (2) `effort=max`/`xhigh` on a non-Opus model passes Aurora's validation but\n124\t  would 400 live (intentional; harmless while effort is default-unset and unwired by roles).\n125\t\n126\t### Wave 7 â€” L5: Model retargeting + tokenizer factor â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n127\t\n