n_count`\n  fold untouched.\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 891 passed (+17). No test weakening.\n- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. Guard verified comprehensive + recursive (catches nested\n  budget_tokens); fold matches Anthropic's real usage semantics (thinking already in output_tokens â†’\n  fold is a correct no-op today, no double-count); mutation-resistant tests (fold-removal under-meter\n  AND double-count over-meter both caught).\n- **TRIPWIRES (LOW, latent, opt-in path only):** (1) the additive thinking-fold could *over*-meter if\n  a future Anthropic usage field duplicates already-counted thinking tokens â€” no current field exists,\n  forward-compat bet; (2) `effort=max`/`xhigh` on a non-Opus model passes Aurora's validation but\n  would 400 live (intentional; harmless while effort is default-unset and unwired by roles).\n\n### Wave 7 â€” L5: Model retargeting + tokenizer factor â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n\n- **Deliverables:** `kb/pricing.yaml` adds `claude-opus-4-8` ($5/$25, verified:true) with L1-style\n  cache sub-rates + `tokenizer_factor: 1.35` (verified:false); `llm.py` `tokenizer_factor`/\n  `estimate_tokens`/`estimate_usd` estimate-only helpers (factor NEVER touches post-call metering â€”\n  ground-truth invariant, regression-pinned).\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 898 passed (+7). No test weakening.\n- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. R1 nothing found (post-call metering provably unfactored;\n  mutation-proven ground-truth test). R2 GO with **honesty findings**: (F1, HIGH-honesty) the\n  estimate helpers are **dead code** â€” no production caller (Aurora budgets in fixed-USD, not token\n  pre-flight), so the tokenizer-factor accuracy goal is not realized; (F2) the defaults were ALREADY\n  on current tiers, so \"retargeting\" changed nothing in the default path. Same inert-plumbing\n  pattern as L2 caching. Corrected an overstated orchestrator comment (F2b).\n- **HONEST OUTCOME / TRIPWIRE:** L5's concrete value is narrow â€” `claude-opus-4-8` is now priced so\n  an `AURORA_*_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8` override meters correctly instead of $0 (closes a $0-fiction\n  hole on the Opus override path) + a deprecated-Opus guard test. The tokenizer factor + estimate\n  helpers are correct, tested, forward-ready, but **inert until a token-budget pre-flight consumer\n  exists**. (F3, LOW: a future 4.7+ model added without the field silently estimates at 1.0.)\n\n### Wave 8 â€” L6: Message Batches API â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n\n- **Deliverables:** `llm.py` `submit_anthropic_batch` + poll/collect + `build_anthropic_request_params`\n  (params identical to the synchronous shape incl. L2 cache / L3 tools / L4 effort + budget_tokens\n  guard) + `_meter_batch_result` (records each result `batch_mode=True` â†’ L1's 0.5Ã— from real usage);\n  `roles/batch_sweep.py` opt-in coordinator (`AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP`, default off); critic_a/reconciler\n  refactored into `build_prompt`/`parse_verdict` + a `prefetched_text` param; orchestrator batches\n  critic_a behind the flag. Per-item failure / timeout / missing result â†’ synchronous degrade\n  (`batch_mode=False`, `_note_degrade`); missing security-judge result â†’ abstain (fail-closed).\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 915 passed (+17). No test weakening.\n- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. Flag-off path verified byte-for-byte (git-diff-confirmed the\n  critic_a/reconciler parse extraction is verbatim; equivalence also guarded by existing\n  test_structured_outputs + test_critic_c); batch metered exactly 0.5Ã—; per-item degrade + ~65-min\n  poll-timeout-degrade + judge fail-closed all tested; budget_tokens guard runs on batch params.\n- **HONEST OUTCOME / TRIPWIRE:** like L2/L5, this is **ready plumbing, not a current win**. Only\n  critic_a is wired (1 of 3 per-candidate Anthropic calls, â‰¤400 tokens); reconciler-batch +\n  judge-batch are built+tested but unwired (reconciler has a hard data-dependency on critic output;\n  judge is on the separate gate path). At TOP_K=2 that's ~2 