{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gyy7PpcTTqZYhspFD3P7Qx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Phase 2 â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready, combined)\n2\t\n3\ttest-command: python -m pytest\n4\t\n5\t**North Star:** Close the two security/judgment tripwires on Aurora's LIVE verdict path AND adopt the\n6\tcheap modern Anthropic capabilities Aurora is missing â€” evolving `llm.py` + the security path, NOT\n7\trebuilding the architecture. Locked-preserved: KB schema + library, single-owner security gate\n8\t(`roles/security/gate.py`), deterministic cost telemetry (CostRecorderâ†’pricing.yaml), Helping Hand +\n9\tpublisher. Both security waves touch the LIVE verdict path: no seam may produce an unearned pass. The\n10\tmetered evidence-shadow batch (SA-1) and the live promotion flip (SA-2) are SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED and\n11\tOUT of these waves. No test weakening; the count may only rise.\n12\t\n13\t> Waves run in series (the threads overlap on `orchestrator.py` + the security judge). Wave 1-2 =\n14\t> security hardening; Wave 3-8 = llm.py upgrades, cost-telemetry substrate first so discount features\n15\t> are metered correctly. Full per-thread rationale + code-grounded findings live in the source plans\n16\t> `docs/AURORA_HARDENING_PLAN.md` and `docs/AURORA_LLM_UPGRADES_PLAN.md`.\n17\t\n18\t## Wave 1 â€” H1: Payload-depth security scan (supersede the served-text backfill)\n19\t\n20\t**Intent:** Replace the W2 served-text baseline (every artifact stamped `clean-with-notes` from\n21\tname + short_description) with a scan of each artifact's real payload, re-fetched from `canonical_url`,\n22\trun through the existing deterministic gate, re-stamping `security_status` so enforce mode reflects\n23\tpayload truth. MONOTONIC toward non-servable. No LLM cost (deterministic detectors only; judge/sandbox\n24\tdefault-off). NOTE (verified): payloads are NOT retained on disk (`payload_files` lazy + empty), so the\n25\tscan must re-fetch â€” but the re-fetch+scan machinery already exists in\n26\t`bin/run_security_shadow.py::_run_pipeline` (real `payload_extractor.extract` â†’ `fetcher.fetch_payload`,\n27\t7-day tarball cache). H1 drives that same scan to ENFORCE-write `security_status`. Scannable set\n28\t(`retired_at IS NULL AND kind IN ('skill','tool','agent','model')`) â‰ˆ 775 artifacts.\n29\t\n30\t**Deliverables:** `bin/scan_payload_depth.py` CLI running the real extractâ†’detectorsâ†’`scorer.score`\n31\tpipeline and persisting via `gate.write_verdict` in enforce mode (`run_judge=False,run_sandbox=False`);\n32\ta monotonic re-stamp guard (reuse `gate._worst_status`, write only when not a relaxation â€” clean\n33\tpayload = `clean-with-notes` = current value, so clean rows untouched; malicious â†’ quarantine/reject);\n34\t`extraction_complete=False` â†’ fail-closed to `quarantine` only when not a relaxation, recorded as\n35\t`extraction-incomplete`; `--limit N`, `--dry-run`, `--audit-out` (lists every verdict changed vs the\n36\tW2 `served-text-v1` backfill); a regression test (benign-name/malicious-payload fixture: `clean-with-notes`\n37\tafter W2, non-servable after payload-depth; a quarantined fixture never relaxed); an adversarial\n38\tno-unearned-pass test (write path can never raise servability) + a CI assertion no new\n39\t`security_status IN (...)` literal is introduced (single-owner test still passes).\n40\t\n41\t**Depends on:** â€”\n42\t\n43\t**done-when:** Every scannable artifact has a payload-depth `security_status` (or audited\n44\t`extraction-incomplete` quarantine); the benign/malicious fixture is caught; the re-stamp is provably\n45\tmonotonic; an audit lists every changed verdict; the single-owner gate test passes; `pytest` green, no\n46\ttest weakening.\n47\t\n48\t- **Given** a benign-description/malicious-payload artifact, **when** the CLI runs in enforce mode, **then** its `security_status` becomes non-servable and it drops out of enforce-mode MCP/publisher queries.\n49\t- **Given** an artifact already stricter-than-clean, **when** the scan computes a milder verdict, **then** the stricter prior holds (worst-wins) â€” no flagged artifact is silently re-admitted.\n50\t- **Given** an unfetchable/stale URL, **then** the result is `extraction-incomplete`, fail-closed where not a relaxation, surfaced in the audit (never left servable on a failed fetch).\n51\t\n52\t## Wave 2 â€” H2: Evidence-loop promotion machinery (real score_fn, engine-diff CLI, tightened gate)\n53\t\n54\t**Intent:** Make the W3 evidence loop promotable: a real per-iteration LLM re-scoring `score_fn` over\n55\tthe payload-deepened corpus (replacing `make_precomputed_score_fn`), a runnable `bin/engine-diff.py`\n56\taround `roles/shadow_diff.py`, and a metered batch to populate `validations_shadow` (0 rows today). The\n57\tflip is NOT performed here â€” the mechanism is wired but defaults to legacy.\n58\t\n59\t**Deliverables:** a real `score_fn` factory in `roles/evidence.py` (beside `make_precomputed_score_fn`)\n60\tthat, given the artifact + a `cost_recorder`, re-runs the critic panel (`critic_a/b/c` â†’ `reconciler`)\n61\tover the current `EvidenceState.corpus` each iteration â€” conservative-bias guard verbatim (loop only\n62\twidens evidence; engine exit rules monotonic toward reject; `score_fn` returns scores, never writes the\n63\tverdict), every critic call metered through `cost_recorder` (no CostRecorder bypass); `bin/engine-diff.py`\n64\tcomputing verdict-match %, the zero-pass-where-legacy-flagged invariant, and a cost ratio, printing\n65\tGO/NO-GO enforcing `agreementâ‰¥0.95`, `min_samplesâ‰¥200`, `unearned==0`, `costâ‰¤1.5Ã—` (add a stricter\n66\tpromotion profile; keep existing constants for back-compat tests); a metered batch command\n67\t(`bin/run_evidence_shadow.py` or `--shadow --limit N --budget-usd C`) running the real loop via\n68\t`shadow_diff.record_shadow` with a hard budget cap (machinery built + unit-tested here; the live run is\n69\tSA-1, OUT of scope); the promotion mechanism wired but defaulting to legacy\n70\t(`AURORA_EVIDENCE_ENGINE=legacy|loop`, default `legacy`, honoring the 1-week `AURORA_ENGINE=legacy`\n71\trollback) â€” this wave swaps the shadow `score_fn` to the real one (still shadow) + adds the default-off\n72\tlive switch; tests (real `score_fn` re-scores on the deepened corpus + meters; non-convergence\n73\tforce-downgrades `pass`â†’`flag`; `bin/engine-diff.py` reports real GO/NO-GO from synthetic shadow rows;\n74\tadversarial test proves no swap can beat legacy leniency without tripping the unearned-pass FAIL;\n75\tsingle-owner gate test still passes).\n76\t\n77\t**Depends on:** Wave 1\n78\t\n79\t**done-when:** `roles/evidence.py` has a real metered per-iteration `score_fn`; `bin/engine-diff.py`\n80\tprints a real GO/NO-GO enforcing all four thresholds; the metered batch command is built + unit-tested;\n81\tthe live switch is wired and defaults to legacy; the loop still structurally cannot emit an unearned\n82\tpass; `pytest` green, no test weakening. The live flip remains a separate authorized step (SA-2).\n83\t\n84\t- **Given** the deepened corpus + real `score_fn`, **then** critics are re-invoked on the wider corpus and every call is metered (no $0 fiction, no bypass).\n85\t- **Given** populated shadow + legacy, **when** `bin/engine-diff.py` runs, **then** it reports match %, unearned count, cost ratio, sample count, and emits GO only if matchâ‰¥95% AND unearned==0 AND samplesâ‰¥200 AND costâ‰¤1.5Ã—.\n86\t- **Given** a non-converging candidate, **then** the verdict force-downgrades to `flag`; the live switch (if enabled) cannot beat legacy leniency without an unearned-pass FAIL.\n87\t\n88\t## Wave 3 â€” L1: Cost-telemetry substrate for cache/batch/new-tokenizer (safety-first)\n89\t\n90\t**Intent:** Extend cost accounting so cache-read, cache-write, and batch-discounted spend can be\n91\tmetered distinctly and correctly BEFORE any feature emits them.\n92\t\n93\t**Deliverables:** migration `kb/migrations/0024_costs_cache_batch.sql` adding nullable `costs` columns\n94\t`cache_read_tokens`, `cache_write_tokens`, `batch_mode INTEGER DEFAULT 0` (mirror in `kb/schema.sql`);\n95\t`kb/pricing.yaml` per-Anthropic-model `cache_read_per_million_usd` (â‰ˆ0.1Ã— input) +\n96\t`cache_write_per_million_usd` (â‰ˆ1.25Ã— input) for sonnet-4-6, haiku-4-5, the new Opus tier (Wave 7),\n97\ta top-level `batch_discount: 0.5`, matching `verification:` entries (verified:false); `llm.py` cache\n98\tsub-rate lookup (same `models/`-prefix robustness + warn-once) + `CostRecorder.record(...)` optional\n99\t`cache_read_tokens=0, cache_write_tokens=0, batch_mode=False` folding cache tokens at their own rates +\n100\tapplying the batch discount (legacy 4-arg call sites byte-for-byte identical); extend\n101\t`tests/test_pricing_keys.py` + new `tests/test_cost_cache_batch.py`.\n102\t\n103\t**Depends on:** Wave 2\n104\t\n105\t**done-when:** `CostRecorder.record` prices cache-read/cache-write/batch spend against matching\n106\tpricing.yaml keys, the legacy 4-arg path is provably unchanged, the two cost tests are green.\n107\t\n108\t- **Given** `cache_read_tokens=N`, **then** those N tokens are priced â‰ˆ0.1Ã— input. [SUBTLE â€” regression test]\n109\t- **Given** `batch_mode=True`, **then** `usd_estimate` is exactly 0.5Ã— the non-batch estimate. [SUBTLE â€” regression test]\n110\t- **Given** a legacy `record(vendor, model, tin, tout)` call, **then** the recorded estimate is identical to pre-wave.\n111\t\n112\t## Wave 4 â€” L2: Prompt caching on repeated critic/judge system+rubric prefixes\n113\t\n114\t**Intent:** Apply `cache_control` to high-repetition system+rubric prefixes (critic_a, security judge,\n115\treconciler) so near-identical nightly prefixes bill at the cache-read rate, metered via Wave 3.\n116\t\n117\t**Deliverables:** `llm.py` `call_anthropic` optional `cache_prefix`/`cache_system` placing\n118\t`cache_control:{\"type\":\"ephemeral\"}` on the system block (structured blocks)