red_outputs.py`.\n147\t\n148\t**Depends on:** Wave 4\n149\t\n150\t**done-when:** Those paths request schema-guaranteed JSON, parse without fence-stripping, an off-schema\n151\tjudge response still fails closed to `abstain`, metering unchanged.\n152\t\n153\t- **Given** a schema-valid response, **then** no `strip_fences` path is taken.\n154\t- **Given** an off-schema/empty judge response, **then** the family is `abstain` and the panel stays fail-closed.\n155\t- **Given** any structured-output call, **then** the cost row matches Wave 3/4 (no `test_pricing_keys` regression).\n156\t\n157\t## Wave 6 â€” L4: Adaptive thinking via `effort` (drop deprecated budget_tokens)\n158\t\n159\t**Intent:** Adopt adaptive thinking through `effort`; never send `budget_tokens` (deprecated on 4.6+;\n160\tOpus 4.8 returns 400); meter thinking tokens correctly.\n161\t\n162\t**Deliverables:** `llm.py` `call_anthropic` `effort: Optional[str]` mapping to the adaptive-thinking\n163\trequest shape; a guard that fails loudly if a `budget_tokens` field is ever assembled for an Anthropic\n164\trequest; fold API-reported thinking tokens into metered output (mirror the Gemini `thoughts_token_count`\n165\tfold â€” root cause of the prior $118 incident); Gemini `thinking_budget=0` guard untouched; optional\n166\tconservative `effort` on critic_a/reconciler/judge (default unset = current behavior); new\n167\t`tests/test_effort_thinking.py`.\n168\t\n169\t**Depends on:** Wave 5\n170\t\n171\t**done-when:** Anthropic path supports `effort`, provably never sends `budget_tokens`, folds thinking\n172\ttokens into metered output, Gemini guard untouched, suite green.\n173\t\n174\t- **Given** any `call_anthropic`, **then** the request contains no `budget_tokens` field. [SUBTLE â€” the 400-on-Opus-4.8 trap]\n175\t- **Given** a response reporting thinking tokens, **then** they are folded into metered output (not dropped).\n176\t- **Given** `effort` unset, **then** behavior + cost identical to pre-wave.\n177\t\n178\t## Wave 7 â€” L5: Model retargeting to current tiers + 4.7+ tokenizer cost factor\n179\t\n180\t**Intent:** Retarget default model tags to current tiers (Opus 4.x / Sonnet 4.6 / Haiku 4.5) and add\n181\tthe ~35%-more-tokens 4.7+ tokenizer factor so cost telemetry stays accurate.\n182\t\n183\t**Deliverables:** `kb/pricing.yaml` add the current Opus tier with cache sub-rates + `verification:`,\n184\treconcile `default_models`/role defaults, add `tokenizer_factor` (default 1.0; 1.35 for 4.7+); `llm.py`\n185\tapply `tokenizer_factor` ONLY to pre-call estimates, NEVER to post-call metering (real `resp.usage`\n186\tstays ground-truth), document the distinction; `orchestrator.py` per-role defaults + role model\n187\tconstants point to retargeted tags via existing `AURORA_*_MODEL` env overrides (no hardcode drift),\n188\t`HAIKU_DEFAULT` stays a real priced tag; extend `tests/test_pricing_keys.py`.\n189\t\n190\t**Depends on:** Wave 6\n191\t\n192\t**done-when:** All default tags resolve to priced keys, the tokenizer factor adjusts estimates only,\n193\t`test_pricing_keys.py` passes with new tags.\n194\t\n195\t- **Given** every retargeted tag, **then** `lookup_rates` hits a non-$0 priced key.\n196\t- **Given** a 4.7+ model, **then** the factor applies to estimates but NOT to recorded actuals. [SUBTLE]\n197\t- **Given** the retargeting, **then** fallback / kill-switch / gate tests stay green.\n198\t\n199\t## Wave 8 â€” L6: Message Batches API for non-interactive nightly sweeps\n200\t\n201\t**Intent:** Opt-in async Message Batches path for the nightly sweeps (~50% discount); synchronous path\n202\tstays the default; correct batch-discounted metering preserved.\n203\t\n204\t**Deliverables:** `llm.py` `submit_anthropic_batch(...)` + poll/collect reusing `_is_retryable_anthropic`,\n205\teach result recording `CostRecorder.record(... batch_mode=True)` from real per-result usage (incl. Wave-4\n206\tcache fields); a single-request batch failure degrades to synchronous `call_anthropic` (`batch_mode=False`)\n207\tvia `_note_degrade` (the sweep never aborts); `orchestrator.py` `walk_pipeline` behind\n208\t`AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP=1` (default off) collecting the per-candidate critic_a/reconciler/judge Anthropic\n209\tcalls into one batch/sweep (flag-off path byte-for-byte the current synchronous pipeline; a missing\n210\tsecurity-judge batch result maps to `abstain`, fail-closed); Gemini path + kill-switch unchanged; new\n211\t`tests/test_batch_sweep.py`.\n212\t\n213\t**Depends on:** Wave 7\n214\t\n215\t**done-when:** The opt-in batch path meters each result at the 50%-discounted rate, degrades per-item on\n216\tfailure, keeps the gate fail-closed, and leaves the default (flag-off) pipeline + all tests unchanged.\n217\t\n218\t- **Given** a collected batch result, **then** its `costs` row has `batch_mode=1` and `usd_estimate` exactly 0.5Ã— the synchronous equivalent. [SUBTLE]\n219\t- **Given** one batched request fails, **then** it falls back to synchronous (metered `batch_mode=0`), the degrade counter increments, the run can close `partial`.\n220\t- **Given** `AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP` unset, **then** pipeline + recorded costs identical to pre-wave; a missing security-judge result fails closed to `abstain`.\n221\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d83a7ead-09bd-4f3c-baca-16f2924a95dc","uuid":"e1495af3-7ff3-4d81-85a5-3cf44730059f","timestamp":"2026-06-17T21:05:41.342Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\aurora\\docs\\foreman-handoff-phase2\\IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md","content":"# Aurora Phase 2 â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready, combined)\n\ntest-command: python -m pytest\n\n**North Star:** Close the two security/judgment tripwires on Aurora's LIVE verdict path AND adopt the\ncheap modern Anthropic capabilities Aurora is missing â€” evolving `llm.py` + the security path, NOT\nrebuilding the architecture. Locked-preserved: KB schema + library, single-owner security gate\n(`roles/security/gate.py`), deterministic cost telemetry (CostRecorderâ†’pricing.yaml), Helping Hand +\npublisher. Both security waves touch the LIVE verdict path: no seam may produce an unearned pass. The\nmetered evidence-shadow batch (SA-1) and the live promotion flip (SA-2) are SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED and\nOUT of these waves. No test weakening; the count may only rise.\n\n> Waves run in series (the threads overlap on `orchestrator.py` + the security judge). Wave 1-2 =\n> security hardening; Wave 3-8 = llm.py upgrades, cost-telemetry substrate first so discount features\n> are metered correctly. Full per-thread rationale + code-grounded findings live in the source plans\n> `docs/AURORA_HARDENING_PLAN.md` and `docs/AURORA_LLM_UPGRADES_PLAN.md`.\n\n## Wave 1 â€” H1: Payload-depth security scan (supersede the served-text backfill)\n\n**Intent:** Replace the W2 served-text baseline (every artifact stamped `clean-with-notes` from\nname + short_description) with a scan of each artifact's real payload, re-fetched from `canonical_url`,\nrun through the existing deterministic gate, re-stamping `security_status` so enforce mode reflects\npayload truth. MONOTONIC toward non-servable. No LLM cost (deterministic detectors only; judge/sandbox\ndefault-off). NOTE (verified): payloads are NOT retained on disk (`payload_files` lazy + empty), so the\nscan must re-fetch â€” but the re-fetch+scan machinery already exists in\n`bin/run_security_shadow.py::_run_pipeline` (real `payload_extractor.extract` â†’ `fetcher.fetch_payload`,\n7-day tarball cache). H1 drives that same scan to ENFORCE-write `security_status`. Scannable set\n(`retired_at IS NULL AND kind IN ('skill','tool','agent','model')`) â‰ˆ 775 artifacts.\n\n**Deliverables:** `bin/scan_payload_depth.py` CLI running the real extractâ†’detectorsâ†’`scorer.score`\npipeline and persisting via `gate.write_verdict` in enforce mode (`run_judge=False,run_sandbox=False`);\na monotonic re-stamp guard (reuse `gate._worst_status`, write only when not a relaxation â€” clean\npayload = `clean-with-notes` = current value, so clean rows untouched; malicious â†’ quarantine/reject);\n`extraction_complete=False` â†’ fail-closed to `quarantine` only when not a relaxation, recorded as\n`extraction-incomplete`; `--limit N`, `--dry-run`, `--audit-out` (lists every verdict changed vs the\nW2 `served-text-v1` backfill); a regression test (benign-name/malicious-payload fixture: `clean-with-notes`\nafter W2, non-servable after payload-depth; a quarantined fixture never relaxed); an adversarial\nno-unearned-pass test (write path can never raise servability) + a CI assertion no new\n`security_status IN (...)` literal is introduced (single-owner test still passes).\n\n**Depends on:** â€”\n\n**done-when:** Every scannable artifact has a payload-depth `security_status` (or audited\n`extraction-incomplete` quarantine); the benign/malicious fixture is caught; the re-stamp is provably\nmonotonic; an audit lists every changed verdict; the single-owner gate test passes; `pytest` green, no\ntest weakening.\n\n- **Given** a benign-description/malicious-payload artifact, **when** the CLI runs in enforce mode, **then** its `security_status` becomes non-servable and it drops out of enforce-mode MCP/publisher queries.\n- **Given** an artifact already stricter-than-clean, **when** the scan computes a milder verdict, **then** the stricter prior holds (worst-wins) â€” no flagged artifact is silently re-admitted.\n- **Given** an unfetchable/stale URL, **then** the result is `extraction-incomplete`, fail-closed where not a relaxation, surfaced in the audit (never left servable on a failed fetch).\n\n## Wave 2 â€” H2: Evidence-loop promotion machinery (real score_fn, engine-diff CLI, tightened gate)\n\n**Intent:** Make the W3 evidence loop promotable: a real per-iteration LLM re-scoring `score_fn` over\nthe payload-deepened corpus (replacing `make_precomputed_score_fn`), a runnable `bin/engine-diff.py`\naround `roles/shadow_diff.py`, and a metered batch to populate `validations_shadow` (0 rows today). The\nflip is NOT performed here â€” the mechanism is wired but defaults to legacy.\n\n**Deliverables:** a real `score_fn` factory in `roles/evidence.py` (beside `make_precomputed_score_fn`)\nthat, given the artifact + a `cost_recorder`, re-runs the critic panel (`critic_a/b/c` â†’ `reconciler`)\nover the current `EvidenceState.corpus` each iteration â€” conservative-bias guard verbatim (loop only\nwidens evidence; engine exit rules monotonic toward reject; `score_fn` returns scores, never writes the\nverdict), every critic call metered through `cost_recorder` (no CostRecorder bypass); `bin/engine-diff.py`\ncomputing verdict-match %, the zero-pass-where-legacy-flagged invariant, and a cost ratio, printing\nGO/NO-GO enforcing `agreementâ‰¥0.95`, `min_samplesâ‰¥200`, `unearned==0`, `costâ‰¤1.5Ã—` (add a stricter\npromotion profile; keep existing constants for back-compat tests); a metered batch command\n(`bin/run_evidence_shadow.py` or `--shadow --limit N --budget-usd C`) running the real loop via\n`shadow_diff.record_shadow` with a hard budget cap (machinery built + unit-tested here; the live run is\nSA-1, OUT of scope); the promotion mechanism wired but defaulting to legacy\n(`AURORA_EVIDENCE_ENGINE=legacy|loop`, default `legacy`, honoring the 1-week `AURORA_ENGINE=legacy`\nrollback) â€” this wave swaps the shadow `score_fn` to the real one (still shadow) + adds the default-off\nlive switch; tests (real `score_fn` re-scores on the deepened corpus + meters; non-convergence\nforce-downgrades `pass`â†’`flag`; `bin/engine-diff.py` reports real GO/NO-GO from synthetic shadow rows;\nadversarial test proves no swap can beat legacy leniency without tripping the unearned-pass FAIL;\nsingle-owner gate test still passes).\n\n**Depends on:** Wave 1\n\n**done-when:** `roles/evidence.py` has a real metered per-iteration `score_fn`; `bin/engine-diff.py`\nprints a real GO/NO-GO enforcing all four thresholds; the metered batch command is built + unit-tested;\nthe live switch is wired and defaults to legacy; the loop still structurally cannot emit an unearned\npass; `pytest` green, no test weakening. The live flip remains a separate authorized step (SA-2).\n\n- **Given** the deepened corpus + real `score_fn`, **then** critics are re-invoked on the wider corpus and every call is metered (no $0 fiction, no bypass).\n- **Given** populated shadow + legacy, **when** `bin/engine-diff.py` runs, **then** it reports match %, unearned count, cost ratio, sample count, and emits GO only if matchâ‰¥95% AND unearned==0 AND samplesâ‰¥200 AND costâ‰¤1.5Ã—.\n- **Given** a non-converging candidate, **then** the verdict force-downgrades to `flag`; the live switch (if enabled) cannot beat legacy leniency without an unearned-pass FAIL.\n\n## Wave 3 â€” L1: Cost-telemetry substrate for cache/batch/new-tokenizer (safety-first)\n\n**Intent:** Extend cost accounting so cache-read, cache-write, and batch-discounted spend can be\nmetered distinctly and correctly BEFORE any feature emits them.\n\n**Deliverables:** migration `kb/migrations/0024_costs_cache_batch.sql` adding nullable `costs` columns\n`cache_read_tokens`, `cache_write_tokens`, `batch_mode INTEGER DEFAULT 0` (mirror in `kb/schema.sql`);\n`kb/pricing.yaml` per-Anthropic-model `cache_read_per_million_usd` (â‰ˆ0.1Ã— input) +\n`cache_write_per_million_usd` (â‰ˆ1.25Ã— input) for sonnet-4-6, haiku-4-5, the new Opus tier (Wave 7),\na top-level `batch_discount: 0.5`, matching `verification:` entries (verified:false); `llm.py` cache\nsub-rate lookup (same `models/`-prefix robustness + warn-once) + `CostRecorder.record(...)` optional\n`cache_read_tokens=0, cache_write_tokens=0, batch_mode=False` folding cache tokens at their own rates +\napplying the batch discount (legacy 4-arg call sites byte-for-byte identical); extend\n`tests/test_pricing_keys.py` + new `tests/test_cost_cache_batch.py`.\n\n**Depends on:** Wave 2\n\n**done-when:** `CostRecorder.record` prices cache-read/cache-write/batch spend against matching\npricing.yaml keys, the legacy 4-arg path is provably unchanged, the two cost tests are green.\n\n- **Given** `cache_read_tokens=N`, **then** those N tokens are priced â‰ˆ0.1Ã— input. [SUBTLE â€” regression test]\n- **Given** `batch_mode=True`, **then** `usd_estimate` is exactly 0.5Ã— the non-batch estimate. [SUBTLE â€” regression test]\n- **Given** a legacy `record(vendor, model, tin, tout)` call, **then** the recorded estimate is identical to pre-wave.\n\n## Wave 4 â€” L2: Prompt caching on repeated critic/judge system+rubric prefixes\n\n**Intent:** Apply `cache_control` to high-repetition system+rubric prefixes (critic_a, security judge,\nreconciler) so near-identical nightly prefixes bill at the cache-read rate, metered via Wave 3.\n\n**Deliverables:** `llm.py` `call_anthropic` optional `cache_prefix`/`cache_system` placing\n`cache_control:{\"type\":\"ephemeral\"}` on the system block (structured blocks), reading\n`usage.cache_read_input_tokens`/`cache_creation_input_tokens` into `CostRecorder.record`; Sonnetâ†’Haiku\nfallback carries the same cache_control; deadline guard + tenacity unchanged; `roles/critic_a.py` +\n`roles/reconciler.py` cache the stable `_SYSTEM`+rubric scaffold (variable tail uncached);\n`roles/security/judge.py` `_call_anthropic_family` caches `_JUDGE_SYSTEM` only (panel/collapse/fail-closed\nuntouched); new `tests/test_prompt_caching.py`.\n\n**Depends on:** Wave 3\n\n**done-when:** Those roles send `cache_control` on stable prefixes, cache tokens metered at Wave-3 rates,\nfallback + tenacity tests still pass.\n\n- **Given** a cached-prefix response reporting cache-read tokens, **then** the `costs` row carries them at â‰ˆ0.1Ã—. [SUBTLE]\n- **Given** a Sonnet failure, **then** the Haiku fallback still carries cache_control and meters correctly.\n- **Given** caching disabled, **then** recorded cost equals pre-wave.\n\n## Wave 5 â€” L3: Structured outputs for critic/security/KB-extraction JSON\n\n**Intent:** Replace brittle `json.loads(strip_fences(...))` with schema-guaranteed JSON on the\ncritic/reconciler/security-judge paths, removing silent parse-failure drops â€” metering + fail-closed\ngate untouched.\n\n**Deliverables:** `llm.py` `output_schema` on `call_anthropic` via the current structured-outputs\nmechanism (metering unchanged); `roles/critic_a.py`, `roles/critic_b.py` (Anthropic-fallback branch\nonly â€” Gemini path keeps its parse), `roles/reconciler.py` one shared verdict schema in\n`roles/contracts.py` (field defaults preserved so abstain/malformed degrades as today);\n`roles/security/judge.py` schema for the `{decision,rationale,cited_field,risk_class}` envelope\n(off-schema â†’ `abstain`, fail-closed); `roles/langextract_adapter.py` (Gemini) stays as-is (out of\nscope); new `tests/test_structured_outputs.py`.\n\n**Depends on:** Wave 4\n\n**done-when:** Those paths request schema-guaranteed JSON, parse without fence-stripping, an off-schema\njudge response still fails closed to `abstain`, metering unchanged.\n\n- **Given** a schema-valid response, **then** no `strip_fences` path is taken.\n- **Given** an off-schema/empty judge response, **then** the family is `abstain` and the panel stays fail-closed.\n- **Given** any structured-output call, **then** the cost row matches Wave 3/4 (no `test_pricing_keys` regression).\n\n## Wave 6 â€” L4: Adaptive thinking via `effort` (drop deprecated budget_tokens)\n\n**Intent:** Adopt adaptive thinking through `effort`; never send `budget_tokens` (deprecated on 4.6+;\nOpus 4.8 returns 400); meter thinking tokens correctly.\n\n**Deliverables:** `llm.py` `call_anthropic` `effort: Optional[str]` mapping to the adaptive-thinking\nrequest shape; a guard that fails loudly if a `budget_tokens` field is ever assembled for an Anthropic\nrequest; fold API-reported thinking tokens into metered output (mirror the Gemini `thoughts_token_count`\nfold â€” root cause of the prior $118 incident); Gemini `thinking_budget=0` guard untouched; optional\nconservative `effort` on critic_a/reconciler/judge (default unset = current behavior); new\n`tests/test_effort_thinking.py`.\n\n**Depends on:** Wave 5\n\n**done-when:** Anthropic path supports `effort`, provably never sends `budget_tokens`, folds thinking\ntokens into metered output, Gemini guard untouched, suite green.\n\n- **Given** any `call_anthropic`, **then** the request contains no `budget_tokens` field. [SUBTLE â€” the 400-on-Opus-4.8 trap]\n- **Given** a response reporting thinking tokens, **then** they are folded into metered output (not dropped).\n- **Given** `effort` unset, **then** behavior + cost identical to pre-wave.\n\n## Wave 7 â€” L5: Model retargeting to current tiers + 4.7+ tokenizer cost factor\n\n**Intent:** Retarget default model tags to current tiers (Opus 4.x / Sonnet 4.6 / Haiku 4.5) and add\nthe ~35%-more-tokens 4.7+ tokenizer factor so cost telemetry stays accurate.\n\n**Deliverables:** `kb/pricing.yaml` add the current Opus tier with cache sub-rates + `verification:`,\nreconcile `default_models`/role defaults, add `tokenizer_factor` (default 1.0; 1.35 for 4.7+); `llm.py`\napply `tokenizer_factor` ONLY to pre-call estimates, NEVER to post-call metering (real `resp.usage`\nstays ground-truth), document the distinction; `orchestrator.py` per-role defaults + role model\nconstants point to retargeted tags via existing `AURORA_*_MODEL` env overrides (no hardcode drift),\n`HAIKU_DEFAULT` stays a real priced tag; extend `tests/test_pricing_keys.py`.\n\n**Depends on:** Wave 6\n\n**done-when:** All default tags resolve to priced keys, the tokenizer factor adjusts estimates only,\n`test_pricing_keys.py` passes with new tags.\n\n- **Given** every retargeted tag, **then** `lookup_rates` hits a non-$0 priced key.\n- **Given** a 4.7+ model, **then** the factor applies to estimates but NOT to recorded actuals. [SUBTLE]\n- **Given** the retargeting, **then** fallback / kill-switch / gate tests stay green.\n\n## Wave 8 â€” L6: Message Batches API for non-interactive nightly sweeps\n\n**Intent:** Opt-in async Message Batches path for the nightly sweeps (~50% discount); synchronous path\nstays the default; correct batch-discounted metering preserved.\n\n**Deliverables:** `llm.py` `submit_anthropic_batch(...)` + poll/collect reusing `_is_retryable_anthropic`,\neach result recording `CostRecorder.record(... batch_mode=True)` from real per-result usage (incl. Wave-4\ncache fields); a single-request batch failure degrades to synchronous `call_anthropic` (`batch_mode=False`)\nvia `_note_degrade` (the sweep never aborts); `orchestrator.py` `walk_pipeline` behind\n`AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP=1` (default off) collecting the per-candidate critic_a/reconciler/judge Anthropic\ncalls into one batch/sweep (flag-off path byte-for-byte the current synchronous pipeline; a missing\nsecurity-judge batch result maps to `abstain`, fail-closed); Gemini path + kill-switch unchanged; new\n`tests/test_batch_sweep.py`.\n\n**Depends on:** Wave 7\n\n**done-when:** The opt-in batch path meters each result at the 50%-discounted rate, degrades per-item on\nfailure, keeps the gate fail-closed, and leaves the default (flag-off) pipeline + all tests unchanged.\n\n- **Given** a collected batch result, **then** its `costs` row has `batch_mode=1` and `usd_estimate` exactly 0.5Ã— the synchronous equivalent. [SUBTLE]\n- **Given** one batched request fails, **then** it falls back to synchronous (metered `batch_mode=0`), the degrade counter increments, the run can close `partial`.\n- **Given** `AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP` unset, **then** pipeline + recorded costs identical to pre-wave; a missing security-judge result fails closed to `abstain`.\n","numLines":221,"startLine":1,"totalLines":221}}}
