{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014p59REePiQT1SZ2WHdJxB9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## foreman-handoff-phase2 â€” grounded summary\n\n**Scope & framing**\n- Phase 2 was an 8-wave Foreman build on branch `foreman/aurora-revamp`, split into two threads: Waves 1â€“2 = security hardening (H1â€“H2) on the live verdict path; Waves 3â€“8 = `llm.py` upgrades (L1â€“L6).\n- North Star (per the plan): close two security/judgment tripwires on the live verdict path AND adopt cheap modern Anthropic capabilities â€” *evolving* `llm.py` + the security path, not rebuilding architecture. Locked-preserved: KB schema + library, single-owner security gate, deterministic cost telemetry, Helping Hand + publisher.\n- Every wave ran EXECUTE â†’ adversarial review (2 independent reviewers) â†’ FIX â†’ re-review, and all 8 converged GREEN in order. Project marked DONE 2026-06-07.\n\n**Ground-truth gate**\n- `python -m pytest` rose from a 752 Phase-1 baseline to **915 passed** (+163 across the 8 waves), with no test weakening anywhere and the security suite green throughout.\n\n**Security thread (Waves 1â€“2) â€” real value**\n- **W1/H1 â€” payload-depth scan:** delivered `bin/scan_payload_depth.py`, which re-fetches each scannable artifact's payload (â‰ˆ775 artifacts; payloads not retained on disk, so it reuses the fetcher's 7-day cache) and runs the real extractâ†’detectorsâ†’scorer path, enforce-writing via `gate.write_verdict`. Re-stamp is provably monotonic (worst-wins via `gate._worst_status`). Honesty fix F1: only genuinely fetched-and-scanned artifacts get `scan_depth: payload-depth`; the â‰ˆ506/775 no-payload artifacts (mostly arxiv) get `served-text-fallback` and keep their value rather than being newly quarantined.\n- **W2/H2 â€” evidence-loop promotion machinery:** delivered a real per-iteration metered `score_fn` in `roles/evidence.py`, `bin/engine-diff.py` (GO/NO-GO enforcing agreementâ‰¥0.95, samplesâ‰¥200, unearned==0, costâ‰¤1.5Ã—), a budget-capped shadow batch runner, and a default-off `AURORA_EVIDENCE_ENGINE=legacy|loop` switch. A BLOCKER-class review catch (both reviewers agreed) found the nightly shadow path had silently been swapped to the real cost-incurring `score_fn`; FIX restored nightly to zero added cost (real re-score gated behind default-off `AURORA_EVIDENCE_LIVE_RESCORE`) and made a $0-shadow â†’ NO-GO.\n\n**llm.py thread (Waves 3â€“8) â€” mixed: some real, some inert plumbing**\n- **W3/L1 â€” cost-telemetry substrate (real, enabling):** migration `0024_costs_cache_batch.sql` adds nullable cache/batch columns; `pricing.yaml` gains cache sub-rates + `batch_discount: 0.5` (all `verified:false`). Legacy 4-arg `CostRecorder.record` path is byte-for-byte unchanged; migration verified idempotent against a live-DB copy preserving 22,013 rows.\n- **W4/L2 â€” prompt caching (HONEST no-op at current sizes):** plumbing is correct and gated behind `cache_prefix_clears_minimum`, but all roles' stable prefixes (15â€“317 tokens) sit 15â€“60Ã— below Anthropic's per-model minimums (Sonnet 2048 / Haiku 4096), so caching never fires today. No cost savings banked; refines the AuroraTwo research's \"#1 cheap win\" to measured-inapplicable.\n- **W5/L3 â€” structured outputs (real robustness):** strict forced tool-use (`emit_result`) with shared verdict/judge schemas; off-schema judge â†’ abstain (fail-closed). Degrades to plain-text parse on any structured-call failure. TRIPWIRE: the no-`required` strict schema is unverified against the live API; until a live smoke confirms, treat L3 as best-effort.\n- **W6/L4 â€” adaptive thinking via `effort` (real safety):** maps to adaptive thinking + per-call effort; a recursive `_assert_no_budget_tokens` guard runs before every Anthropic dispatch (Opus 4.8 400s on `budget_tokens`), and thinking tokens are folded into metered output (guards the $118-incident class). Default (effort unset) is cost-neutral.\n- **W7/L5 â€” model retargeting + tokenizer factor (mostly inert):** prices `claude-opus-4-8` ($5/$25, verified:true) with cache sub-rates + `tokenizer_factor: 1.35`. Honesty findings: the estimate helpers are dead code (no production caller â€” Aurora budgets in fixed-USD, not token pre-flight), and defaults were already on current tiers. Concrete value is narrow: an Opus override now meters correctly instead of $0.\n- **W8/L6 â€” Message Batches API (ready, not a current win):** opt-in `AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP` coordinator (default off) with 0.5Ã— metering, per-item synchronous degrade, judge fail-closed. Only critic_a is wired; at TOP_K=2 that's ~2 small calls/night (sub-cent), and the ~65-min blocking poll makes enabling it net-negative EV at current scale.\n\n**Net honest outcome & follow-ups**\n- Real wins: H1, H2, L1, L3, L4. L2/L5/L6 are correct, honest, forward-ready plumbing that is **largely inert** at Aurora's current prompt sizes + TOP_K=2 â€” exactly the research's \"validate before banking\" caveat, now measured.\n- **SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED, not run:** H2 SA-1 (metered shadow batch to populate `validations_shadow` â‰¥200) and SA-2 (live evidence-engine flip); the live H1 payload re-stamp against `kb/aurora.db`. All gated, default-off.\n- Open tripwires/follow-ups: L3 live-schema smoke test; W2-R2-4 candidate-filter lacks a dedicated regression test (LOW); L4 forward-compat over-meter risk if a future Anthropic usage field duplicates thinking tokens.\n- Commits 0eca5f2 (W1) Â· ffae677 (W2) Â· 2618f59 (W3) Â· 0a24914 (W4) Â· f046810 (W5) Â· e604fa4 (W6) Â· 7b23c9e (W7) Â· +W8. **Not pushed; awaiting John's review.**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":920,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13932,"cache_read_input_tokens":33665,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13932},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent